# Patterns for secret scanners to skip. One regular expression per line
# (RE2/Go syntax, the format TruffleHog's --exclude-paths parses). NOT
# gitignore-glob syntax. See robotsix-standards
# docs/secret-files-are-never-tracked.md.
#
# TruffleHog (shared python-security.yml workflow) reads this file directly via
# --exclude-paths. detect-secrets does NOT read it; if a detect-secrets hook is
# added to .pre-commit-config.yaml, mirror these paths in its `exclude:` regex.
#
# Add a pattern here when a tracked file triggers a false positive, rather
# than adding it to .gitignore.

# Lockfile: package hashes are high-entropy strings, not secrets.
^uv\.lock$

# Test fixtures: shared respx mocks with synthetic tokens/payloads.
^tests/(.*/)?conftest\.py$
^tests/fixtures/
